text #47081\n\nJan 17, 2026 · 0 comments\n\nDiscussion options\n\n## \n\nl4b4r4b4b4 Jan 17, 2026\n\n## Problem\n\nWhen working on long coding sessions with the Agent panel, the context window fills up (e.g., 8k/129k tokens used). Currently there's no way to start a fresh chat session while preserving the thread context/history reference. This forces users to either:\n\n  1. Continue in a bloated context (slower, may hit limits)\n  2. Start a completely new thread and lose all context\n  3. Manually create handoff notes and start fresh\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nAdd ability to \"checkpoint\" or \"branch\" a new chat session from an existing agent thread, where:\n\n  * New session starts with fresh context window\n  * Previous thread remains accessible/linkable\n  * Optional: Allow attaching a summary or key context from previous session\n\n## Use Case\n\nLong development sessions (like multi-session project scaffolding) where:\n\n  * Session 1-6 build up significant context\n  * Session 7 needs fresh context but benefits from thread continuity\n  * User wants to reference prior sessions without carrying full token weight\n\n## Additional Context\n\nWorking on a multi-session project where each session adds ~4-5k lines of code. By session 7, context management becomes the bottleneck rather than the actual development work.\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n## Replies: 0 comments\n\nSign up for free to join this conversation on GitHub. Already have an account? Sign in to comment\n\n💡 Feature Requests\n\nLabels\n\nNone yet\n\n1 participant\n\nConverted from issue\n\nThis discussion was converted from issue #47040 on January 17, 2026 22:30.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - forkgitss/kohya-ss-musubi-tuner · GitHub (https://github.com/forkgitss/kohya-ss-musubi-tuner)\nciteturn30970search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; GitHub Discussions Enabled: We've enabled GitHub Discussions for communi