 asked this question in Q&A\n\nSchema migration should increase minor version #11096\n\nJan 17, 2026 · 1 comment\n\nDiscussion options\n\n## \n\ngpongelli Jan 17, 2026\n\n### Description\n\nHi,\nI'm using authelia since months, recently I've upgraded from 4.39.10 to v4.39.15.\nOn this last version I'm facing issue with safari on iOS I'll open a bug.\nTo try solve I've tried go back to 4.39.10 but I got this error:\n    \n    `time=\"2026-01-17T18:22:21+01:00\" level=info msg=\"Authelia v4.39.10 is starting\"\n    time=\"2026-01-17T18:22:21+01:00\" level=info msg=\"Log severity set to info\"\n    time=\"2026-01-17T18:22:25+01:00\" level=info msg=\"Storage schema is being checked for updates\"\n    time=\"2026-01-17T18:22:29+01:00\" level=error msg=\"Error occurred running a startup check\" error=\"error during schema migrate: current schema version is greater than the latest known schema version, you must downgrade to schema version 22 before you can use this version of Authelia\" provider=storage\n    time=\"2026-01-17T18:22:31+01:00\" level=fatal msg=\"One or more providers had fatal failures performing startup checks, for more details check the error level logs\" providers=\"[storage]\" stack=\"github.com/authelia/authelia/v4/internal/commands/root.go:93 (*CmdCtx).RootRunE\\ngithub.com/spf13/cobra@v1.10.1/command.go:1015               (*Command).execute\\ngithub.com/spf13/cobra@v1.10.1/command.go:1148               (*Command).ExecuteC\\ngithub.com/spf13/cobra@v1.10.1/command.go:1071               (*Command).Execute\\ngithub.com/authelia/authelia/v4/cmd/authelia/main.go:10      main\\ninternal/runtime/atomic/types.go:194                         (*Uint32).Load\\nruntime/asm_arm64.s:1268                                     goexit\"\n    `\n\nSo, in case there is a Storage schema change, considering the numbering scheme `major.minor.patch` , is it possible to increase the minor version instead of the patch version ?\nSo people can understand there's a greater difference that cannot be reverted easily. thanks.\n\n### Use Case\n\nas human, being able to understand that a schema change was made between releases.\n\n### Details\n\nNo response\n\n### Documentation\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\nAdmin verified this answer by Crowley723 Jan 17, 2026\n\nWe adhere to semantic versioning which generally means that a major release introduces breaking changes, a minor release is non-breaking with new features, and a patch release is bug fixes or minor features/enhancements.\n\nI don't think that artificially bumping the minor version every time we introduce a storage migration is a great idea. We also publish updates to our documentation when storage migrations are added. (See here)\n\nThat said, we do provide migrations to go back to a lower migration. (See here.)\n\nView full answer\n\nCrowley723 Jan 17, 2026\n\nWe adhere to semantic versioning which generally means that a major release introduces breaking changes, a minor release is non-breaking with new features, and a patch release is bug fixes or minor features/enhancements. I don't think that artificially bumping the minor version every time we introduce a storage migration is a great idea. We also publish updates to our documentation when storage migrations are added. (See here) That said, we do provide migrations to go back to a lower migration. (See here.)\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n0 replies\n\nAnswer verified by Admin Jan 17, 2026\n\nCategory\n\n💭 Q&A\n\nLabels\n\npriority/4/normal Normal priority items type/feature Request for adding a new feature status/needs-design Requires formal design process via a discussion or feature request\n\n\nConverted from issue\n\nThis discussion was converted from issue #11094 on January 17, 2026 21:45.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRunning Copilot coding agent · louislam/its-mytabs@d409bd7 · GitHub (https://github.com/louislam/its-mytabs/actions/ru